<p>Wind damage claims in San Antonio rarely come from hurricanes. Most come from thunderstorms. The NOAA Storm Events Database lists 309 thunderstorm wind reports and 71 tornado reports in Bexar County, and many of the worst events were short, violent downbursts that hit a few square miles hard and left the next neighborhood alone. That patchy pattern is one reason insurers sometimes question whether wind really caused the damage. Wind also tends to arrive with hail and heavy rain in the same storm, so a single claim may involve several kinds of damage that each need to be documented and priced.</p>
<p>This page explains how wind claims work, what insurers look for, and how a public adjuster in San Antonio may help you present the loss. For a longer guide, read <a href="/wind-damage-insurance-claims-san-antonio-tx/">wind damage insurance claims in San Antonio</a>.</p>

